+// bringUp drives the actor to RUNNING (ewallet patch). Upstream treated RESUMING and SUSPENDING
+// as "needs nothing" and waited for RUNNING, which never came when the suspend was still in
+// flight. Callers normally hold the session's turn, so these states come only from another
+// process or from an ate-api workflow still finishing after its caller gave up:
+//   - SUSPENDING: complete (or join) the suspend first, then resume;
+//   - RESUMING, SUSPENDED, UNSPECIFIED, PAUSED, PAUSING: ResumeActor (ate-api's resume workflow
+//     is re-entrant, so an abandoned RESUMING is finished on the worker it already holds);
+//   - Aborted (another workflow holds the actor): wait for it to settle, then decide again.
+//
+// Other states (CRASHED) are left to the reachability wait, as upstream. Bounded by ctx.
+func (b *SandboxAgentActorBackend) bringUp(ctx context.Context, atespace, actorID string, st ateapipb.Actor_Status) error {
